class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}(T,X,X)\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}(T,X,X)\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"58-df-function\">58-df-function</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Contraction}_S:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{Contraction}_S:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}contraction} \\vdash \\mathrm{Contraction}_S(T,X,d)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S(X,d)\\land\\mathrm{Function}(T,X,X)\\land\\exists c\\in[0,1)\\;\\forall x,y\\in X\\;(d(T(x),T(y))\\leq c\\,d(x,y))\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}contraction} \\vdash \\mathrm{Contraction}_S(T,X,d)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S(X,d)\\land\\mathrm{Function}(T,X,X)\\land\\exists c\\in[0,1)\\;\\forall x,y\\in X\\;(d(T(x),T(y))\\leq c\\,d(x,y))\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Contractions are the maps used in Banach fixed-point arguments.</li>\n<li>The carrier and metric are arguments of the predicate, so the same graph <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\">\\(T\\)</span> cannot inherit a contraction constant from an unrelated metric witness.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-metric-space","status":"resolved","id":"ce876585d129ce97","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-metric-space]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-function","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"",